#. type: Title =
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-backfill.adoc:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "git-backfill(1)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-backfill.adoc:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "NAME"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-backfill.adoc:7
msgid "git-backfill - Download missing objects in a partial clone"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-backfill.adoc:10
#, no-wrap
msgid "SYNOPSIS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-backfill.adoc:13
msgid "git backfill [--min-batch-size=<n>] [--[no-]sparse]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-backfill.adoc:15
#, no-wrap
msgid "DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-backfill.adoc:24
msgid ""
"Blobless partial clones are created using `git clone --filter=blob:none` and "
"then configure the local repository such that the Git client avoids "
"downloading blob objects unless they are required for a local operation.  "
"This initially means that the clone and later fetches download reachable "
"commits and trees but no blobs. Later operations that change the `HEAD` "
"pointer, such as `git checkout` or `git merge`, may need to download missing "
"blobs in order to complete their operation."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-backfill.adoc:30
msgid ""
"In the worst cases, commands that compute blob diffs, such as `git blame`, "
"become very slow as they download the missing blobs in single-blob requests "
"to satisfy the missing object as the Git command needs it. This leads to "
"multiple download requests and no ability for the Git server to provide "
"delta compression across those objects."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-backfill.adoc:37
msgid ""
"The `git backfill` command provides a way for the user to request that Git "
"downloads the missing blobs (with optional filters) such that the missing "
"blobs representing historical versions of files can be downloaded in "
"batches. The `backfill` command attempts to optimize the request by grouping "
"blobs that appear at the same path, hopefully leading to good delta "
"compression in the packfile sent by the server."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-backfill.adoc:44
msgid ""
"In this way, `git backfill` provides a mechanism to break a large clone into "
"smaller chunks. Starting with a blobless partial clone with `git clone --"
"filter=blob:none` and then running `git backfill` in the local repository "
"provides a way to download all reachable objects in several smaller network "
"calls than downloading the entire repository at clone time."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-backfill.adoc:47
msgid ""
"By default, `git backfill` downloads all blobs reachable from the `HEAD` "
"commit. This set can be restricted or expanded using various options."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-backfill.adoc:49
msgid "THIS COMMAND IS EXPERIMENTAL. ITS BEHAVIOR MAY CHANGE IN THE FUTURE."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-backfill.adoc:52
#, no-wrap
msgid "OPTIONS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-backfill.adoc:54
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--min-batch-size=<n>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-backfill.adoc:59
msgid ""
"Specify a minimum size for a batch of missing objects to request from the "
"server. This size may be exceeded by the last set of blobs seen at a given "
"path. The default minimum batch size is 50,000."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-backfill.adoc:60
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--sparse`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-backfill.adoc:61
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--no-sparse`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-backfill.adoc:65
msgid ""
"Only download objects if they appear at a path that matches the current "
"sparse-checkout. If the sparse-checkout feature is enabled, then `--sparse` "
"is assumed and can be disabled with `--no-sparse`."
msgstr ""

